WEBVTT

00:01.770 --> 00:02.980
After the scrolling words had disappeared,

00:04.440 --> 00:09.300
I was still waiting for it to keep going

00:07.110 --> 00:07.570
My Teenage Romcom SNAFU

00:07.110 --> 00:07.570
Climax

00:20.200 --> 00:24.590
Those six words that everyone knows

00:24.590 --> 00:29.590
that decorate the last page of all those famous fairy tales

00:30.920 --> 00:35.430
You've just slapped them on the end

00:35.430 --> 00:41.400
And declared everything to have a happy ending

00:41.400 --> 00:42.770
One by one everyone leaves their seats

00:47.420 --> 00:49.320
Happily ever after

00:52.030 --> 00:57.120
And even after the credits end

00:57.120 --> 01:03.220
The screen still won't show me what happens next

01:05.070 --> 01:09.300
If this story is to end

01:12.550 --> 01:14.720
I hope it ends with not snow but rain

01:14.720 --> 01:20.570
That way I can still cast my eyes to the sky

01:20.570 --> 01:24.360
Even if it leaves me soaked, the rain will surely

01:24.360 --> 01:29.980
Have blessed another's blossoming

01:31.490 --> 01:33.610
Did you hear that a new trendy café opened?

01:33.610 --> 01:34.970
Oh yeah, I have.

01:34.970 --> 01:36.440
The one that serves bubble tea?

01:36.440 --> 01:39.240
No, that one's already passé.
Unless you're an old guy, maybe.

01:39.240 --> 01:42.670
What? But my brother seems to like it a lot...

01:49.850 --> 01:50.460
Here you go.

01:50.460 --> 01:51.200
Thank you!

01:51.200 --> 01:52.080
Thank you very much!

01:52.080 --> 01:53.520
Cheers!

01:56.950 --> 01:58.060
Thanks.

02:00.960 --> 02:02.850
Seems like no one's coming.

02:02.850 --> 02:05.560
If we knew there was no job to do, we wouldn't bother coming here.

02:05.560 --> 02:06.680
That's true.

02:06.680 --> 02:09.690
And since you're free, I can give you work for the student council, right?

02:09.690 --> 02:10.930
No thanks.

02:10.930 --> 02:12.260
Also, what are you doing here?

02:12.260 --> 02:13.320
You're not a member.

02:13.320 --> 02:17.600
Yes, but it's simply good business to wine and dine a regular client, right?

02:17.600 --> 02:18.800
Showa-era thinking!

02:18.800 --> 02:20.040
Speaking of!

02:20.040 --> 02:23.680
The student council's budget is tight because of last year's expenses.

02:23.680 --> 02:25.540
We need you to make up the difference.

02:25.540 --> 02:27.640
Isn't that, like, almost all your fault though?

02:28.250 --> 02:29.840
I'm talking about the prom <i>we</i> did.

02:29.840 --> 02:32.720
Y-Yeah, sure, sorry about that.

02:32.720 --> 02:35.680
I need to find some stray freshmen
to help. Or some stray cats, even.

02:35.680 --> 02:37.760
Oh? Wanna borrow ours?

02:37.760 --> 02:39.430
He's super adorable.

02:39.430 --> 02:42.020
No, I wasn't being serious.

02:42.020 --> 02:43.600
You sure 'bout that?

02:43.600 --> 02:45.960
Then, shall I lend you my paws?

02:45.960 --> 02:48.040
Whoa, you startled me!

02:49.480 --> 02:51.820
Your hands are so warm, Yukino!

02:52.960 --> 02:54.560
Can't you do something about it?

02:54.560 --> 02:58.160
Dunno. Maybe. You should ask the club president.

02:58.160 --> 03:01.520
You're right. Getting a cat is a great idea.

03:01.520 --> 03:03.000
I think the club should get one too.

03:03.000 --> 03:04.480
You're not even listening!

03:04.480 --> 03:05.840
Komachi, wake up!

03:05.840 --> 03:07.320
Come home! Pspspsps!

03:08.320 --> 03:09.360
That was close!

03:09.360 --> 03:11.630
I almost fell asleep!

03:13.560 --> 03:15.930
Anyway, I think the club president should decide.

03:15.930 --> 03:17.610
Good call!

03:21.080 --> 03:22.200
Wait, me?

03:22.200 --> 03:23.680
I'll have to decide everything?!

03:23.680 --> 03:25.200
Don't worry about a thing.

03:25.200 --> 03:26.440
We'll help you, too.

03:26.440 --> 03:27.440
Yui!

03:28.480 --> 03:30.160
Is that fine by you?

03:30.160 --> 03:32.280
Uh, I guess. We always manage somehow.

03:33.440 --> 03:34.860
Here you go.

03:42.040 --> 03:43.410
Are you some grade-school bully?

03:43.840 --> 03:45.870
Did you forgot about our plans for the evening?

03:46.600 --> 03:48.170
If only I <i>could</i> forget.

03:48.170 --> 03:50.360
Something bad happen?

03:50.360 --> 03:51.500
You could say that.

03:51.500 --> 03:53.400
Now that I think about it...

03:53.400 --> 03:54.880
Do you know something, rice girl?

03:54.880 --> 03:57.380
Yes, a li'l birdie called Haruno told me something.

03:57.380 --> 04:00.200
Why are you getting info from <i>that</i> particular source?

04:00.200 --> 04:02.310
I'm not up to date on all these leaks.

04:02.310 --> 04:06.080
Basically, my brother is gonna have dinner with Yukino's mother tonight.

04:06.080 --> 04:07.440
Oh, I see...

04:07.440 --> 04:08.120
Huh.

04:08.120 --> 04:09.840
Whoa, don't try so hard to seem interested!

04:09.840 --> 04:11.940
I'm not interested in the slightest, in fact.

04:11.940 --> 04:15.040
Well, now that you mention it, you look pretty rough.

04:15.040 --> 04:15.800
You think?

04:15.800 --> 04:17.800
It's the usual dead look.

04:17.800 --> 04:18.840
See? Like usual.

04:18.840 --> 04:19.820
Which part?

04:19.820 --> 04:22.160
Well, I get how you feel.

04:22.160 --> 04:24.830
I wouldn't be happy having to go eat dinner with that old hag either.

04:24.830 --> 04:27.160
Ha—?! Watch your mouth!

04:27.160 --> 04:29.480
Whoa, you're so wonderful when you trash talk, Iroha!

04:29.480 --> 04:31.330
Please adopt me already, mommy!

04:31.330 --> 04:33.450
Don't call me that. It's weird.

04:34.090 --> 04:35.880
You're going to have dinner in a few, right?

04:35.880 --> 04:37.320
This is off-limits.

04:37.320 --> 04:39.000
Speaking of, shouldn't you go get ready?

04:39.000 --> 04:40.800
We'll clean up the room for you.

04:40.800 --> 04:42.390
O-Okay.

04:42.390 --> 04:44.000
I'll leave it to you all, then.

04:44.000 --> 04:45.000
Thanks.

04:47.930 --> 04:49.760
We'll be leaving early today.

04:49.760 --> 04:50.680
See you tomorrow.

04:50.680 --> 04:52.730
Gotcha! See you tomorrow!

04:52.730 --> 04:54.480
Oh, Yukino!

04:54.480 --> 04:56.360
You left this behind!

04:59.200 --> 05:01.040
Thanks, you're a lifesaver.

05:01.040 --> 05:02.340
Don't mention it!

05:03.880 --> 05:05.440
I wonder if Bro's gonna be okay.

05:05.440 --> 05:07.280
I don't think we have to worry too much.

05:07.280 --> 05:10.410
That's what I thought, but Haruno's gonna be with them too.

05:10.410 --> 05:14.680
Ouch, then he's gonna be in big trouble. I'm betting one perica they're having a big fight on the way home.

05:14.680 --> 05:18.400
Then I'm betting he's gonna head to the bathroom and never come out!

05:18.400 --> 05:19.880
Yui, what are you betting on?

05:19.880 --> 05:24.400
I'll pass on the betting... But I think they're not gonna fight at all.

05:24.400 --> 05:26.040
Oh, you think so?

05:26.040 --> 05:28.800
I thought those two got into fights all the time.

05:28.800 --> 05:30.280
Not at all!

05:30.280 --> 05:32.960
Heated discussions aren't a problem at all!

05:32.960 --> 05:35.480
At most they won't talk to each other for two weeks, IMO.

05:35.480 --> 05:37.560
The hell?! That's like the worst that can happen!

05:37.560 --> 05:39.820
Augh, they'll be even more of a pain to be around...

05:39.820 --> 05:42.960
Yeah, that stupid couple is so annoying to deal with.

05:42.960 --> 05:45.070
My brother <i>alone</i> is annoying.

05:47.740 --> 05:49.950
C'mon now, we just have to believe in them!

05:49.950 --> 05:51.720
Y-You really think so?

05:51.720 --> 05:53.280
Yeah, you'll get used to it!

05:53.280 --> 05:55.920
Things are like that between them <i>all the time</i>!

05:56.320 --> 05:59.710
Uhm, all-knowing Iroha, how do I quit the club?

05:59.710 --> 06:02.600
I'm not a member of the club, so who knows!

06:02.600 --> 06:04.200
Maybe the prez can help somehow.

06:04.200 --> 06:05.660
Oh wait, that's you!

06:05.660 --> 06:07.430
Welp, it's student council 'o clock!

06:07.430 --> 06:09.760
No, please, don't leave me alone!

06:09.760 --> 06:12.040
Hey, what the hell are you doing?! Let go!

06:12.040 --> 06:14.820
You have no idea how much work's on my plate for the next two weeks!

06:14.820 --> 06:16.570
Don't leave me!

06:16.570 --> 06:18.760
I don't think we should worry too much!

06:19.480 --> 06:21.680
Eh? You <i>really</i> think so?

06:21.680 --> 06:23.300
Yep! Pinky promise.

06:23.300 --> 06:25.790
Hikki won't get too mad, probably.

06:25.790 --> 06:28.120
He'll just be so tired he'll look dead for a couple days.

06:29.370 --> 06:34.000
Though, on the other hand, Yukinon will get caught up in her thoughts and eventually do something drastic.

06:35.440 --> 06:39.480
We're so blessed to have Yui in our club.
I don't want to imagine where we'd be without her.

06:39.480 --> 06:41.260
You finally realized it, huh?

06:41.830 --> 06:43.880
I wonder if Yukinon's gonna be okay...

06:44.210 --> 06:46.200
She's just like an angel, scary.

06:46.200 --> 06:48.050
More like a goddess, you mean.

06:48.480 --> 06:50.260
So, where are we going?

06:50.260 --> 06:52.200
It's a restaurant my family often frequents.

06:52.200 --> 06:54.200
Bet it's gonna be hella expensive then.

06:54.200 --> 06:55.900
I wonder if I'm meeting their dress code.

06:55.900 --> 06:59.270
It's a casual place. You don't have to worry at all.

06:59.270 --> 07:00.920
A simple school uniform is fine.

07:00.920 --> 07:02.320
Aight, I see.

07:02.320 --> 07:04.200
Oh shoot, I forgot my tie!

07:04.200 --> 07:05.280
I'll have to go home to get it.

07:05.280 --> 07:07.110
Though I'm not sure I'm coming back.

07:07.110 --> 07:08.580
No need to worry.

07:08.580 --> 07:10.420
Komachi already thought of that.

07:14.710 --> 07:16.560
We're good to go!

07:25.300 --> 07:28.000
<i>Come on, </i>you<i> decided to do it, don't blush now!</i>

07:28.000 --> 07:29.550
<i>I'm gonna start blushing too!</i>

07:30.160 --> 07:34.350
Making him meet up with her parents...
She's building the road to marriage, huh?

07:34.350 --> 07:36.320
Y-You think?

07:36.320 --> 07:38.690
He also met my mother...

07:38.690 --> 07:41.540
You for real? This guy, I swear...

07:41.540 --> 07:45.680
Well, if you build a road to my brother's heart,
he'll probably just put up spike strips.

07:45.680 --> 07:46.680
Yep, utter trash.

07:46.680 --> 07:48.400
Not even good for compost, I'm telling you!

07:48.400 --> 07:51.240
Uhm, yeah, I guess he really is trash...

07:51.240 --> 07:52.240
Indeed!

07:52.240 --> 07:57.080
He's a worthless piece of silent garbage that becomes
a word machine-gun when he needs to spit out excuses!

07:57.080 --> 07:58.720
I wasn't really going for that.

07:58.720 --> 08:01.000
You quite enjoy the trash talk, rice girl.

08:01.750 --> 08:04.720
I think you should take matters into your own hands, Yui.

08:04.720 --> 08:07.010
Yeah, but you see, it's kinda...

08:07.010 --> 08:11.760
You came back to the club in the first place because you were mentally prepared for all this, am I right?

08:11.760 --> 08:14.890
Uhm, yeah, you're right, sure.
Exactly how things went.

08:15.320 --> 08:17.480
But...

08:17.480 --> 08:21.040
It's impossible to think about anything else when I'm near those two!

08:21.040 --> 08:22.770
Y'all really are a pain in the ass, huh.

08:25.280 --> 08:28.560
Wouldn't it demotivate you if they started being all lovey dovey and flirty all the time?

08:28.560 --> 08:32.440
Remember, only by stealing other people's things can you feel that they are truly yours.

08:32.440 --> 08:33.870
What?! You're scary!

08:34.700 --> 08:36.760
Komachi, what do you think about this?

08:36.760 --> 08:39.870
Don't you hate it when your brother gets tangled up in stuff like this?

08:39.870 --> 08:43.360
I'm not involved in the slightest,
so you're all welcome to put up a fight!

08:43.360 --> 08:46.400
I'll even set up a bloody girlfriend battle royale to decide who gets him!

08:46.400 --> 08:48.380
Wha—she's even worse than Iroha!

08:48.380 --> 08:50.120
Don't worry, we're just kidding.

08:50.120 --> 08:51.560
Yep, from start to finish.

08:52.880 --> 08:55.640
I wouldn't mind if you two stopped teasing me like this...

09:01.100 --> 09:02.400
<i>I'm being tested.</i>

09:02.400 --> 09:04.480
<i>I'm being appraised right now.</i>

09:04.480 --> 09:06.680
Well then, shall we start?

09:08.000 --> 09:09.650
By the way, Yukino...

09:09.650 --> 09:12.110
How has school been going lately?

09:12.110 --> 09:14.370
Well, you know, the usual.

09:14.980 --> 09:17.400
Don't mind us, Hikigaya.
You can start eating now.

09:17.400 --> 09:18.770
Sure...

09:20.290 --> 09:23.040
<i>Which one is it?!
Which damn pair do i use?!</i>

09:23.040 --> 09:24.920
Well then, I'm going in!

09:26.040 --> 09:27.550
Sho yummy!

09:29.720 --> 09:32.080
Hikigaya, you're supposed to use the outer—

09:32.080 --> 09:36.720
C'mon, you shouldn't whisper your sweet nothings in front of your mom and sister!

09:36.720 --> 09:38.880
They shouldn't do it even if not in front of us.

09:38.880 --> 09:41.440
Yukino, what were you thinking?

09:41.440 --> 09:43.730
Hikigaya, I really mean it, go right ahead.

09:48.110 --> 09:50.480
And Haruno, where are your manners?

09:50.480 --> 09:52.680
Cutlery should be used from the outside in.

09:52.680 --> 09:54.740
Oh whoops, guess I messed up!

09:55.080 --> 09:57.990
Hikigaya, you certainly know your table manners, don't you?

09:57.990 --> 10:00.080
Yeah, well...

10:00.080 --> 10:03.000
<i>That was close! How many traps has this old hag set up?!</i>

10:03.000 --> 10:05.040
Your etiquette is surprisingly refined.

10:05.040 --> 10:07.880
Your parents must have done an excellent job teaching you.

10:07.880 --> 10:09.900
Well, I guess they were
better than you, at least.

10:13.160 --> 10:16.360
Pick your words with a modicum of care, you fool.

10:16.360 --> 10:19.040
Right, I'm sorry, I was just being the usual unfiltered me.

10:19.040 --> 10:21.270
But can you blame me? You two look the same.

10:21.270 --> 10:24.600
It's fine, really. Makes both of us feel more at ease.

10:24.600 --> 10:26.190
But you really are something, eh?

10:28.190 --> 10:32.240
In my experience, being cautious'll just increase the distance between you and him.

10:32.240 --> 10:34.480
It's like you're trying to be nice to him.

10:34.480 --> 10:38.720
You're being careful because you want to "get along."
But that's not just what you're aiming for, is it?

10:38.720 --> 10:40.680
I mean, I guess not...

10:40.680 --> 10:41.640
Right?!

10:41.640 --> 10:43.840
That's why you attack when things are still awkward!

10:43.840 --> 10:46.080
Oh, a line worthy of the Romance Master title!

10:47.080 --> 10:49.330
No wonder things went <i>so</i> smoothly with Hayama!

10:49.800 --> 10:52.050
What? Where'd you hear about that?

10:52.050 --> 10:54.130
Who is it? Hachiman? It's him, isn't it?!

10:54.130 --> 10:55.820
<i>When things are awkward...</i>

10:54.130 --> 10:55.060
Did he tell you?

10:55.060 --> 10:56.230
No, no!

10:56.230 --> 10:59.060
So basically, Hayama and Tobe were talking about it,

10:59.060 --> 11:01.680
and without even realizing he let that slip out...

11:01.680 --> 11:02.360
Okay, let's kill him.

11:02.360 --> 11:03.310
We kill him?

11:03.310 --> 11:04.810
Yes, you're right!

11:04.810 --> 11:06.770
Right?! Let's kill him!

11:10.190 --> 11:13.200
I'm sorry we're the only ones drinking.

11:10.980 --> 11:15.980
My Teenage
Romcom SNAFU
Climax

11:13.200 --> 11:14.520
No, it's no problem at all.

11:14.520 --> 11:17.200
We have a family thing of being good drinkers.

11:17.200 --> 11:19.910
Though you're probably way weaker because of your father, Yukino.

11:19.910 --> 11:21.840
Do I truly resemble Father that much?

11:21.840 --> 11:24.400
Of course you do! Like how you're such a pain to deal with!

11:24.400 --> 11:25.870
Look who's talking.

11:25.870 --> 11:27.580
Well, you're the same too.

11:29.290 --> 11:32.120
Hikigaya, which one of your parents do you resemble the most?

11:32.120 --> 11:34.800
Well, if I had to pick one, I'd say my father as well.

11:34.800 --> 11:36.720
The only thing I got from my mother is the hair.

11:36.720 --> 11:39.750
Then Komachi's cowlick is from Mother too?

11:39.750 --> 11:41.180
I guess so.

11:41.180 --> 11:44.790
Also, don't call my mom <i>that</i>. It's kinda weird.

11:44.790 --> 11:45.910
You mean Mother?

11:45.910 --> 11:48.400
Yeah, it feels weird. I'm not used at all.

11:48.810 --> 11:50.320
I-I see.

11:50.320 --> 11:52.190
It feels nice to say, though...

11:52.190 --> 11:53.960
Who's this Komachi you're speaking of?

11:53.960 --> 11:55.490
She's my younger sister.

11:55.490 --> 11:56.900
The best in the world!

11:56.900 --> 11:58.280
What a coincidence!

11:58.280 --> 12:00.280
I also have the best younger sister in the world!

12:00.280 --> 12:02.080
Sis, please, you're embarrassing me.

12:02.080 --> 12:04.200
I see, so you're the eldest?

12:04.200 --> 12:05.790
Huh? Yes, that's right.

12:06.680 --> 12:09.210
I see. This'll work out, then.

12:09.640 --> 12:10.580
What will?

12:11.200 --> 12:13.680
By the way, do you know our family business?

12:13.680 --> 12:15.970
From all these questions, detective agency?

12:19.760 --> 12:21.440
Good lord, that was funny!

12:21.440 --> 12:23.930
So, is it safe to say you two are dating?

12:27.680 --> 12:29.000
Would that be... okay?

12:29.000 --> 12:30.880
I'm not the person you should be asking.

12:30.880 --> 12:35.000
Haruno, it'd be pretentious to want a yes from me now, right?

12:52.040 --> 12:53.480
So, what happened yesterday?

12:53.480 --> 12:56.070
So, based off of what Haruno told me...

12:56.070 --> 12:56.800
Mumble mumble mumble.

12:56.800 --> 12:58.380
Ah, I knew it!

12:58.380 --> 13:00.320
Rice girl, you gotta pay the one perica I bet!

13:00.320 --> 13:02.800
Right now?! Plus, how do I even get perica?

13:02.800 --> 13:05.560
All right! That's it for today. Let's go home!

13:11.350 --> 13:12.770
Garbroge, I gotta say...

13:12.770 --> 13:15.770
Yes, sorry, it probably is my fault.

13:15.770 --> 13:17.150
At least you're aware.

13:17.150 --> 13:18.340
Yeah.

13:18.340 --> 13:20.570
I feel like I messed up big time.

13:20.570 --> 13:24.660
Since it felt like I was talking to Yukino,
I said a lot of things that shouldn't be said.

13:24.660 --> 13:27.320
I don't think that's a surprise to anyone.

13:27.320 --> 13:28.540
Right.

13:28.540 --> 13:33.000
Garbroge, you never say the important stuff, but you'll happily say the wrong thing at the wrong time.

13:33.000 --> 13:35.790
Hmm, at times like this... I guess I should apologize?

13:36.250 --> 13:38.240
Give her some Toraya sweets while prostrating?

13:38.240 --> 13:40.800
I don't think you need to go that far.

13:40.800 --> 13:43.010
But still, I think you need to do right by her.

13:43.010 --> 13:46.180
I see, then I guess some Orandaya snacks will suffice.

13:46.180 --> 13:48.500
Huh? That's not what I meant, really...

13:48.500 --> 13:49.930
Hikki!

13:49.930 --> 13:52.350
Are you free now? You're free, right? Free now, right?!

13:52.350 --> 13:53.130
Yay, I knew it!

13:53.130 --> 13:54.880
Calm down, Speediyama Gonzales.

13:54.880 --> 13:56.950
At least wait for my answer.

13:56.950 --> 14:00.760
Whoops, I just remembered something I really need to buy!

14:00.760 --> 14:02.780
Hey, wait! I want to choose the sweets!

14:02.780 --> 14:05.010
Don't even think about it, you utterly foolish Hachiman!

14:05.010 --> 14:07.740
Don't worry, leave it to me!

14:07.740 --> 14:09.700
All right, I'm going!

14:11.370 --> 14:13.900
Well, looks like I'm free now.

14:13.900 --> 14:14.740
Aight, going home?

14:14.740 --> 14:15.920
We're not going home!

14:16.630 --> 14:18.620
Hikki, let's go on a date.

14:22.550 --> 14:23.970
Where are we going?

14:23.970 --> 14:25.550
It's a secret!

14:30.550 --> 14:32.180
The aquarium?

14:34.650 --> 14:36.260
You sure about this?

14:36.260 --> 14:37.080
Yep!

14:38.700 --> 14:40.440
A shark!

14:40.440 --> 14:41.990
It's been a while.

14:41.990 --> 14:44.020
Really? I came here the other day.

14:44.020 --> 14:45.910
Long time no see, Hammerhead.

14:45.910 --> 14:47.780
He was talking to the shark!

14:50.380 --> 14:52.040
Wanna take a picture?

14:52.040 --> 14:53.680
Oh? Sure thing, thanks!

14:55.890 --> 14:56.980
O-Oh, wait!

14:59.060 --> 15:00.210
Hey...

15:01.630 --> 15:03.130
Now, what's next?

15:12.520 --> 15:15.940
It says that with their strong healthy teeth, they can crunch on the hardest things.

15:15.940 --> 15:18.060
Yep, that's sure what the words say.

15:18.060 --> 15:19.440
Yeah.

15:19.860 --> 15:23.440
Though, sometimes, words aren't enough.

15:28.280 --> 15:30.380
Oh, how have you been?

15:30.380 --> 15:32.970
It's so rough. Almost feels like shark teeth.

15:32.970 --> 15:34.120
Right?

15:34.580 --> 15:37.830
You may be right, words sometimes don't do things justice.

15:38.830 --> 15:41.920
Oh, the penguins! Hikki, wanna go?

15:46.220 --> 15:48.730
Oh, I have no idea what they're doing, but they're hella cute!

15:48.730 --> 15:51.590
I gotta send Komachi thousands of cute pics!

15:57.100 --> 15:58.770
--- Penguin 1

15:57.100 --> 15:58.770
-- Mask

15:57.100 --> 15:58.770
-- Text

15:57.100 --> 15:58.770
.  Have you noticed two of the penguins cuddling?
Those two are actually mates.
.  Once two Humboldt penguins mate, they tend to stay
with the same partner until one of them dies.
They show their affection by grooming their partner's
body and calling out to them. We hope you enjoy
observing the couple's behavior.

15:57.100 --> 15:58.770
Are you curious about the relationship between the two penguins?

15:57.100 --> 15:58.770
Humboldt Penguins

15:58.770 --> 16:01.770
--- Penguin 2

15:58.770 --> 16:01.770
-- Mask

15:58.770 --> 16:01.770
-- Text

16:05.060 --> 16:06.860
What should we do now?

16:06.860 --> 16:07.860
Go home, I guess.

16:07.860 --> 16:09.570
I don't mean that.

16:12.860 --> 16:14.700
I mean about Yukinon

16:14.700 --> 16:17.370
and about me.

16:18.100 --> 16:19.550
In short, about us three.

16:31.820 --> 16:34.640
Really... thanks for fulfilling my wish.

16:34.640 --> 16:37.950
But I really didn't do anything, I mean it.

16:37.950 --> 16:41.440
Plus, the only way we still got a club is because of you, Yui.

16:41.440 --> 16:43.150
That's not true at all.

16:43.700 --> 16:50.200
If you hadn't been honest, I don't think we'd be able to talk to each other face to face like this.

16:51.110 --> 16:53.330
But, you know what?

16:54.360 --> 16:57.580
I really wish you'd hurt my feelings.

16:58.710 --> 16:59.660
That's...

16:59.660 --> 17:02.400
I hate when you only do things halfway.

17:02.910 --> 17:03.880
Sorry.

17:03.880 --> 17:06.360
I hate when you just make assumptions.

17:06.360 --> 17:07.510
I'm sorry.

17:07.510 --> 17:10.890
I also hate that you're not making up excuses now that I'm angry.

17:10.890 --> 17:14.940
I hate it when you say useless things and not the important stuff.

17:14.940 --> 17:15.810
Well...

17:15.810 --> 17:19.430
And I don't like that Yukinon refuses to ask important questions.

17:19.870 --> 17:22.300
Even though I can still blame that on you.

17:22.300 --> 17:23.490
Guess you're right.

17:24.010 --> 17:24.860
But...

17:33.970 --> 17:36.460
Even taking all of that in account...

17:36.460 --> 17:38.160
I love you.

17:48.720 --> 17:52.550
I'm sorry I can't give a proper answer.

17:53.240 --> 17:58.760
I know I'm super pathetic, but I feel like I'm missing entire pages of dictionaries to convey what I feel.

17:59.350 --> 18:00.680
It's fine.

18:00.680 --> 18:03.220
I just wanted to tell you.

18:03.220 --> 18:04.940
Make of it what you want.

18:05.540 --> 18:08.190
So, one day, words will come on their own.

18:08.900 --> 18:10.210
Yuigahama...

18:10.210 --> 18:14.450
My feeling won't change, until I give up.

18:14.450 --> 18:17.290
So don't force a reply now.

18:17.290 --> 18:20.690
If I get annoying, burdensome,
or just too much of a nuisance...

18:20.690 --> 18:24.330
You can just smile or cry,
and run away, like you always do.

18:24.740 --> 18:29.460
<i>I'm sure that someday, someone will confess to her their feelings in a similar way.</i>

18:29.460 --> 18:31.840
<i>A confession full of mistakes.</i>

18:32.860 --> 18:34.890
I don't think I'll be able to run away.

18:34.890 --> 18:37.390
Yep! I won't ever let you run away!

18:41.140 --> 18:42.770
Yukino, this is for you!

18:44.520 --> 18:46.140
This might not be much—

18:46.140 --> 18:47.780
Yeah, it's not much, it's the best.

18:47.780 --> 18:49.530
You shut your mouth, Bro.

18:49.530 --> 18:51.820
Now go ahead, Yukino, open it!

18:53.610 --> 18:54.700
I wonder what it is.

18:54.700 --> 18:58.700
Well, your family recently treated my brother at a good restaurant, so think of this as a thank you!

18:58.700 --> 19:00.010
I chose it with him.

19:00.010 --> 19:01.280
With Hikigaya?

19:01.280 --> 19:03.830
Uhm, well, yeah...

19:03.830 --> 19:07.750
About the way I behaved with your mother the other day—I should've picked better replies.

19:07.750 --> 19:08.750
I'm really sorry.

19:08.750 --> 19:09.890
I see.

19:13.090 --> 19:14.880
Wait, what are you doing?

19:14.880 --> 19:18.450
You should do this kind of thing next time you see my mother.

19:18.450 --> 19:19.720
There's going to be a next time?

19:19.720 --> 19:20.970
Of course.

19:20.970 --> 19:24.440
Anyway, since we're here,
why don't we eat this together?

19:24.440 --> 19:25.540
You sure?

19:25.540 --> 19:26.690
Yay!

19:26.690 --> 19:29.130
Oh, I love sweets from that place!

19:29.130 --> 19:31.150
Hmm, this is my first time trying 'em.

19:36.730 --> 19:37.660
You're bullying me again?

19:37.660 --> 19:39.660
I'm not bullying, just training.

19:39.660 --> 19:41.510
Hikigaya, sit. Beg.

19:41.510 --> 19:44.120
No need to talk to me like a dog.
I behave at home, anyway.

19:44.120 --> 19:46.750
<i>Home</i> is exactly where you guys should be doing whatever this is.

19:46.750 --> 19:49.340
He gets the same discipline from me at home!

19:49.340 --> 19:51.130
Ew, what kind of siblings are you?

19:51.130 --> 19:52.120
What'd you just say?!

19:52.120 --> 19:53.020
How rude!

19:53.020 --> 19:55.920
Then we'll have to take him for a walk.

19:55.920 --> 19:58.490
I suppose I can take him out this weekend...

19:58.490 --> 19:59.510
I'm not coming.

19:59.510 --> 19:59.890
Huh?

19:59.890 --> 20:00.480
Huh?

20:00.480 --> 20:02.930
Do you have any plans, then? See, you're free.

20:02.930 --> 20:04.530
You didn't give me time to answer.

20:04.530 --> 20:07.440
Freestyle is all about respect.
Follow the rules. Rules!

20:13.730 --> 20:16.400
That's no good, Yukinon!

20:17.140 --> 20:19.210
If you don't hold tight to it,

20:19.210 --> 20:20.620
I might swipe it away!

20:33.960 --> 20:36.440
My. Who knew a thief was among us?

20:36.440 --> 20:38.680
It's my property, you know.

20:38.680 --> 20:41.460
I wonder, who knows for sure!

20:41.460 --> 20:43.950
If you loosen your grip a little, I might take it!

20:43.950 --> 20:45.810
I'm very greedy, after all.

20:45.810 --> 20:46.810
Everyone, stop!

20:46.810 --> 20:48.500
The one with more stuffing is mine.

20:48.500 --> 20:50.240
Why are you standing up?

20:50.240 --> 20:51.810
We told you, sit down!

20:51.810 --> 20:52.970
Here, take this.

20:52.970 --> 20:54.320
Thanks.

20:57.550 --> 20:59.070
Want some milk for your tea?

20:59.070 --> 21:01.700
Yes, let's make it thick, like him.

21:04.710 --> 21:07.870
Yeah, thick is right.

21:12.440 --> 21:14.070
C'mon, this is the last one!

21:14.670 --> 21:15.710
It's so good!

21:15.710 --> 21:18.720
Well of course, the brand's a Chiba specialty.

21:18.720 --> 21:22.650
You see, I'm the type of person to try out lots of things!

21:22.650 --> 21:23.640
I'll give you this!

21:24.330 --> 21:27.890
What do you mean you're giving it to me? Huh? What?

21:28.170 --> 21:29.680
It's tasty, y'know!

21:31.580 --> 21:35.650
There's nothing tastier than someone else's dish!

21:37.380 --> 21:38.140
Hikigaya.

21:38.140 --> 21:39.320
Hikki.

21:42.360 --> 21:43.360
Komachi, let's split it.

21:43.360 --> 21:44.280
Hey, wait!

21:44.280 --> 21:47.530
No, don't cut it! I won't be able to eat half brother!

21:47.530 --> 21:48.700
I'm not that bad!

21:57.120 --> 21:57.960
Come in!

22:01.930 --> 22:05.930
So, Adolescence Never Ends,

22:01.930 --> 22:05.930
and My Youth Marches On.
